---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Map from '../components/Map.astro';
import Filters from '../components/Filters.astro';
import HowItWorks from '../components/HowItWorks.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import { events } from '../data/content.json';
const entries=events;
const topics=[...new Set(entries.map(item=>item.topic))];
const regions=[...new Set(entries.map(item=>item.region))];
---
<Shell title="Civilization Timeline"><section class="intro"><span class="motif" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="intro-top"><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>{entries.length} records</span></div> <h1 class="editorial">{learning.heading}</h1> <p>{entries.length} selected events across {regions.length} regions.</p></section><Filters topics={topics} regions={regions} timeline/><HowItWorks><p>Compare periods, explore learning and trade, and keep the source beside each event.</p><p><strong>Map.</strong> Land outlines give regional orientation. No historical state borders or exact event locations are plotted.</p><p><strong>Comparing events.</strong> Overlapping bands do not prove contact or causation. Broad periods and exact years retain different precision.</p></HowItWorks><div class="collection-tools"><h2 id="entries">Choose an event</h2> <button class="button secondary" id="copy-saved">Copy my list</button></div> <div class="timeline-list">{entries.map(item=><><article class="panel timeline-record" data-item-id={item.id} data-search={`${item.title} ${item.place} ${item.summary}`} data-topic={item.topic} data-region={item.region} data-start={item.start} data-end={item.end}><div class="timeline-date">{item.date}<div class="date-ribbon" aria-hidden="true"><span style={`margin-left:${(item.start-650)/1010*100}%;width:${Math.max(.5,(item.end-item.start+1)/1010*100)}%`}></span></div></div> <div><div class="tag-row"><span class="pill">{item.region}</span> <span class="pill neutral">{item.topic}</span></div><h2 class="top-gap"><a data-reading-link={item.id} href={`/event/${item.id}/`}>{item.title}</a></h2><p>{item.summary}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/event/${item.id}/`}>Read the event</a> <button class="button secondary" data-save={item.id} aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div></div></article>{' '}</>)}</div> <div id="empty" class="empty" hidden><h2>Nothing matches</h2><p>Try fewer words, change a filter, or turn off “Saved only.”</p></div><section class="panel panel-body top-gap"><h2>Map</h2><Map/><div class="region-keys" aria-label="Filter by region">{regions.map(region=><><button data-region-filter={region}>{region}</button>{' '}</>)}</div></section><section class="panel panel-body top-gap"><h2>At the same time…</h2><div class="compare-controls"><label class="field">First event<select id="compare-a">{entries.map(item=><option value={item.id}>{item.title}</option>)}</select></label> <label class="field">Second event<select id="compare-b">{entries.map((item,index)=><option value={item.id} selected={index===1}>{item.title}</option>)}</select></label> <button class="button" id="compare">Compare periods</button></div> <div id="comparison" role="status"></div></section><script>import "../lib/library";import "../lib/timeline";</script></Shell>